    kernels/core: add fused MXFP4->BF16 CUDA dequant, Rust dispatch, and tests
    
    - candle-kernels: add fused CUDA kernel dequant_mxfp4_to_bf16 that decodes FP4 (E2M1) two nibbles per byte, per 32-elem block, multiplies by E8M0 scale via exp2f(int8), casts to BF16 and writes to output. Supports layout: blocks [rows, cols/32, 16], scales [rows, cols/32], outputs BF16 [rows, cols].
    
    - candle-core/mxfp4:
      - add shape validation helper,
      - implement dequant_mxfp4_to_bf16_cuda (CUDA-only) and dequant_mxfp4_to_bf16 (CPU/CUDA dispatch),
      - keep CPU implementation for fallback/testing.
    
    - tests: add mxfp4_cuda.rs with:
      - CPU/GPU parity test on 8x256 (BF16 bit-equality),
      - short throughput sanity micro-benchmark.
    
    Notes:
    - Phase A dequant-on-load path; uses IEEE754 semantics for FP4 E2M1 and E8M0.
    - Built with --release; parity test passes; throughput test runs quickly.
    - No API breakage; unrelated CUDA qmm tests remain unchanged.

commit 7a6152604670b495318b565a9d14286e2c36d6ce
Author: user <user@user.user>
Date:   Sun Oct 19 13:01:36 2025 +0200

    candle-core: add MXFP4 CPU dequantization to BF16 + tests
    
    Introduce dequant_mxfp4_to_bf16_cpu(blocks, scales, [rows, cols]) which decodes MXFP4 (FP4 E2M1 + E8M0) blocks into a contiguous BF16 weight matrix on CPU.
    
    Validation: \n- Enforces cols % 32 == 0 and shapes blocks=[rows, cols/32, 16], scales=[rows, cols/32].\n- Low nibble -> column 2*j, high nibble -> column 2*j+1.\n- FP4 E2M1 decode incl. subnormals; scales via pow2(i8).\n- Cast to BF16 (RNE) and place row-major.
    
    Tests: \n- T3 Reconstruction: quantize a 4x64 synthetic matrix to MXFP4 in-test, dequant with the new fn; assert MAE<0.20, MSE<0.08.\n- T4 Layout: 3x96 case validates last-dim blocking and nibble order (exact BF16 match).
    
    Also exposes module via lib.rs. All candle-core tests pass locally; no new warnings.

